data/libritts_speakers.json is derived from LibriTTS-P by LINE Corporation
(https://github.com/line/LibriTTS-P), the speaker identity prompts in data/df1_en.csv,
data/df2_en.csv and data/df3_en.csv, and its excluded_spk_list.txt. The gender field is the
annotators' majority; the description is annotator 1's, with annotators 2 and 3 as fallback;
the gender words themselves were removed from the description.

LibriTTS-P is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Citation:
  Masaya Kawamura, Ryuichi Yamamoto, Yuma Shirahata, Takuya Hasumi, Kentaro Tachibana.
  "LibriTTS-P: A Corpus with Speaking Style and Speaker Identity Prompts for Text-to-Speech
  and Style Captioning." Interspeech 2024.
